BT 1 0 0 1 0 49.5 Tm /F1 10.5 Tf 15 TL (The Pharmacy Inventory System is a console-based Java application that manages medicines and their) Tj T* (stock for a small pharmacy. It is a beginner-level Data Structures and Algorithms \(DSA\) project that) Tj T* (combines hashing, a Binary Search Tree \(BST\), sorting, a linked list and file handling in one practical) Tj T* (program.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 56 604.8898 cm
q
BT 1 0 0 1 0 79.5 Tm 15 TL /F1 10.5 Tf 0 0 0 rg (A HashMap stores every medicine against its medicine ID so that a medicine can be found in constant) Tj T* -0.093189 Tw (average time. A BST organises the medicines by name, and an in-order traversal of the tree lists them in) Tj T* 0 Tw (alphabetical order. Sorting is used to prepare expiry-date and price reports. Every stock change \(adding) Tj T* (a medicine, restocking and selling\) is recorded as a stock transaction in a singly linked list. Medicines) Tj T* (and transactions are loaded from the data file ) Tj /F2 10.5 Tf (pharmacy.txt) Tj /F1 10.5 Tf ( when the program starts and saved back) Tj T* (when the program exits.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 56 553.8898 cm
q
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 34.5 Tm /F1 10.5 Tf 15 TL (The program enforces simple business rules: the price of a medicine must be greater than zero, the) Tj T* (stock can never become negative and a sale cannot exceed the available stock. The project uses a text) Tj T* (file instead of a database, which keeps the scope suitable for a college-level submission.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
