BT 1 0 0 1 0 64.5 Tm /F1 10.5 Tf 15 TL -0.034827 Tw (Pharmacies handle hundreds of medicines, each with its own price, stock level and expiry date. Keeping) Tj T* 0 Tw -0.106377 Tw (these records on paper makes it slow to find a medicine, easy to miss a low-stock item and risky to sell a) Tj T* 0 Tw (medicine that has expired or is no longer available. A small computerised inventory system solves these) Tj T* (problems by keeping the records organised and by checking every operation before it changes the) Tj T* (stock.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 56 360.8898 cm
q
BT 1 0 0 1 0 64.5 Tm 15 TL /F1 10.5 Tf 0 0 0 rg (This project demonstrates the idea on a small scale. The pharmacist chooses an option from a menu:) Tj T* (add a medicine, search, sell, restock, display all medicines or view the low-stock and expiry reports. The) Tj T* (program validates the input, finds the medicine using the HashMap or the BST, updates the stock,) Tj T* (records a transaction in the linked list and prints the result. When the pharmacist exits, all data is written) Tj T* (back to ) Tj /F2 10.5 Tf (pharmacy.txt) Tj /F1 10.5 Tf (.) Tj T* ET
